{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20370",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 1.22,
      "end_seconds": 5.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "So, hello, doctor. May I come in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.23,
      "end_seconds": 11.88,
      "duration_seconds": 4.65,
      "text": "You're alright, take a seat. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 17.45,
      "end_seconds": 24.84,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Okay, so doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.73,
      "end_seconds": 28.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Absolutely, come and sit beside them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.38,
      "end_seconds": 41.45,
      "duration_seconds": 11.07,
      "text": "Actually, mainly a cough that won't go away. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.16,
      "end_seconds": 45.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "What's on your current medicine list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.61,
      "end_seconds": 51.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I'm on Foracort inhaler, twice a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.36,
      "end_seconds": 72.33,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "How long has this been bothering you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 73.59,
      "end_seconds": 83.69,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "It's been about two weeks, I'm fairly sure. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.58,
      "end_seconds": 95.63,
      "duration_seconds": 10.05,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.39,
      "end_seconds": 111.58,
      "duration_seconds": 14.19,
      "text": "It's on and off. A seven out of ten, I suppose. Sorry, I know I'm rambling a bit. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.67,
      "end_seconds": 117.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Have you noticed anything else alongside it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 117.84,
      "end_seconds": 137.32,
      "duration_seconds": 19.48,
      "text": "It usually comes with a bit of a sore throat. And I've been getting breathless on the stairs as well, for two days. Okay, so about getting breathless on the stairs, pretty moderate, if I'm being honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.15,
      "end_seconds": 143.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "did you get weight loss, night sweats or sharp chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.7,
      "end_seconds": 151.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.12,
      "text": "Erm, no weight loss, night sweats or sharp chest pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.87,
      "end_seconds": 153.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.84,
      "text": "Any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 159.17,
      "end_seconds": 161.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.82,
      "text": "No, um, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 163.67,
      "end_seconds": 169.48,
      "duration_seconds": 5.81,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. He doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 170.91,
      "end_seconds": 178.1,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.63,
      "end_seconds": 185.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.13,
      "text": "alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed any leg swelling or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.93,
      "end_seconds": 190.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.78,
      "text": "No, none of those at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.45,
      "end_seconds": 194.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.05,
      "end_seconds": 203.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "yeah, no, nothing like that"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.86,
      "end_seconds": 207.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.21,
      "end_seconds": 225.8,
      "duration_seconds": 16.59,
      "text": "I've, I've had asthma, yes. Mm, uh, I've had acid reflux for about ten years now. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.97,
      "end_seconds": 235.52,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "alright, acid reflux, that matches what I have here right, what line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.18,
      "end_seconds": 243.03,
      "duration_seconds": 5.85,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.13,
      "end_seconds": 245.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "How active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 247.5,
      "end_seconds": 251.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.85,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 261.14,
      "end_seconds": 264.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Okay, did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 269.8,
      "end_seconds": 274.77,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Well, I had my tonsils removed as a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.47,
      "end_seconds": 279.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.29,
      "end_seconds": 282.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.59,
      "text": "Not to my knowledge, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.14,
      "end_seconds": 286.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.01,
      "end_seconds": 295.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.66,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.8,
      "end_seconds": 323.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "Okay: SpO2 97 percent on room air, blood pressure 127 over 70, temp 36.9 degrees, pulse 75, respiratory rate 15."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.32,
      "end_seconds": 330.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.96,
      "text": "Let me look at the area, I'll be gentle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 331.57,
      "end_seconds": 334.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "I'm just checking this side."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 341.42,
      "end_seconds": 345.62,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "the chest is clear and your oxygen level is normal"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 356.56,
      "end_seconds": 358.41,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Yes, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 362.23,
      "end_seconds": 380.99,
      "duration_seconds": 18.76,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again so where does that leave us? It points towards a lingering cough after a viral infection the reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together we shouldn't forget cough-variant asthma"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 381.91,
      "end_seconds": 384.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "So, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 385.5,
      "end_seconds": 407.0,
      "duration_seconds": 21.5,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's a lingering cough after a viral infection, and we'll know more once the a chest X-ray is back. So, to recap quickly. You've had a cough that won't go away for about two weeks, and no weight loss or sharp chest pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.12,
      "end_seconds": 409.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "yes, that's right"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.71,
      "end_seconds": 420.26,
      "duration_seconds": 8.55,
      "text": "I'll request a chest X-ray, it'll help with persistent cough i think a breathing test makes sense here, for breathlessness"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 421.82,
      "end_seconds": 424.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "do I need to prepare?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 425.61,
      "end_seconds": 450.36,
      "duration_seconds": 24.75,
      "text": "Let's use salbutamol inhaler, 100 micrograms, two puffs when needed, for two weeks. That's for wheeze and cough. Honey and lemon in warm water can ease it, and avoid smoky rooms. If you cough up blood or get breathless at rest, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department. Let's plan a check in three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 450.9,
      "end_seconds": 451.6,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 452.69,
      "end_seconds": 455.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.44,
      "text": "Does all of that make sense?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 456.38,
      "end_seconds": 459.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 462.88,
      "end_seconds": 464.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.37,
      "text": "Take care now."
    }
  ]
}